Source: p9share
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: David Walther <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/moebiusV/9share
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: p9share
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, openssh-client, kmod
Recommends: openssh-server
Description: share directories between machines over 9P, through ssh
 One command on the machine that has the files (p9share export DIR HOST)
 and one on the machine that shows them (sudo p9share mount USER NAME DIR).
 The machine with the files dials out with ssh, so the other needs no open
 port.  A root daemon, started at boot, keeps the tunnels up and the mounts
 right (read-write, read-only or off, switched by the user without sudo).
 .
 Includes daud, a 9P2000.L file server forked from diod.  Does nothing until
 something is configured.
